{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>A people fierce.</b> We do not know whether the nun is a root letter or for the nif'al pattern, and it is a foreign word with no family [of cognates]. The meaning is a foreign or strange people. And the one who says that the nun stands in place of lamed is not correct:" "<b>A stammering tongue.</b> For every tongue that a person does not understand is in his eyes a mockery:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:31.284956990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}